.TH VEYON-INPUT-HELPER 8 2026-11-26 VEYON
.SH NAME
veyon-input-helper \- Veyon input blocking helper for Wayland sessions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B veyon-input-helper
.I PID
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B veyon-input-helper
blocks the keyboard and the mouse while Veyon locks the screen of a Wayland
session: Veyon Server (\fBveyon-server\fP) starts it with its own process ID,
and only that process may tell it, through the socket
\fI/run/veyon/input-block.sock\fP, to grab or release the input devices in
\fI/dev/input\fP. It is not meant to be run by hand. X11 sessions do not use
it.
.PP
It needs root privileges. Upstream installs it setuid root; this package does
not (see \fI/usr/share/doc/veyon-master/README.Debian\fP). To block input in
Wayland sessions, make it setuid root with:
.PP
.RS
dpkg-statoverride --update --add root root 4755 /usr/bin/veyon-input-helper
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR veyon-server (1),
.BR veyon-service (1)
.PP
.I https://veyon.io/
.SH AUTHOR
Veyon has been written by Tobias Junghans. This manual page has been written
